  "id": "probability-value",
  "term": "probability value",
  "definition": "A probability value, or p value, is the chance of getting a result at least as different from what the null hypothesis specifies as the result actually observed, assuming the null hypothesis is true. Smaller p values indicate stronger evidence against the null hypothesis, and they may be calculated for one-tailed or two-tailed tests.",
